WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.556
Welcome to Module 3 of the
HR-Driven Identity learning path:

2
00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:06.763
make joiners ready on day one.

3
00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:12.151
This is Gate 3, Joiners, with
Chapter 03 of the developer workbook.

4
00:00:12.151 --> 00:00:15.476
Modules 1 and 2 settled who
writes each account state,

5
00:00:15.476 --> 00:00:18.575
and brought contractors
in from their own source.

6
00:00:18.575 --> 00:00:20.537
Now the new hire's first morning.

7
00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:25.321
In this module you'll keep the Lifecycle
Workflows definitions as reviewed files,

8
00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:29.541
lint them before they reach the tenant,
plan each change against what the

9
00:00:29.541 --> 00:00:34.113
tenant already holds, and measure how many
hires were actually ready on day one.

10
00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:37.123
You'll also see why the
Temporary Access Pass a new

11
00:00:37.123 --> 00:00:39.987
hire gets should be
short-lived and one-time use.

12
00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:43.400
The code runs on your laptop
against fictional fixtures.

13
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.770
It's illustrative: unit-tested against
fixtures, not run against a live tenant.
